 1380 f8a9:             ;
 1381 f8a9:             ; the CRTC registers R0..R15 for vinit, as measured on the card 2026-10-21: an 11.0592 MHz crystal (Q2, SV4 on 1-2),
 1382 f8a9:             ; 6 dots a character (IC28 a 74163), 8 scan lines a row (RA0..2): a 1.8432 MHz character clock, 117 characters a line
 1383 f8a9:             ; = 63.5 us (15.75 kHz), 32 rows + 6 lines = 262 lines (60.1 Hz), non-interlaced - a TV-rate monitor. 80 columns
 1384 f8a9:             ; (43.4 us of text) fit such a monitor's visible ~48 us with a margin each side (R2 94 centres them); a 9 MHz crystal
 1385 f8a9:             ; gave room for only 64. The character EPROM gets ~540 ns a character (an MBM2732A is a 450 ns part). R1/R6 follow
 1386 f8a9:             ; VROWS; tools/vidsim.py timing checks a table.
 1387 f8a9:             ; 2026-10-22: R0..R3 per card (vmode picks one, R6), R4..R15 common. A V1.3 card runs from 12 MHz: 6 dots a 2.0 MHz
 1388 f8a9:             ; character, 127 a line (15.75 kHz), 80 x 24 (40 us of text, R2 98 centres it); 8 dots a 1.5 MHz character, 95 a line
 1389 f8a9:             ; (15.79 kHz), 64 x 24 - the 64-column table proven on the monitor 2026-10-21 (then from 9 MHz / 6, the same 1.5 MHz).
 1390 f8a9:             ; 2026-11-10 (branch video-v2): the V2.0 card, 12 MHz like the V1.3; the V1.0-V1.2 table (11.0592 MHz: 116, 80, 94, 9)
 1391 f8a9:             ; is gone with the card.
 1392 f8a9:             ; V4 (docs/cards/video-v4.md section 3): 640 x 480 at 60 Hz with the text in a band of 400 lines. A count is 16
 1393 f8a9:             ; dots of the 25.175 MHz oscillator, 635.6 ns: 50 counts a line (31.469 kHz), 32 rows of 16 lines and 13 lines (525
 1394 f8a9:             ; lines, 59.94 Hz); both syncs negative, which is control 2 = 0. tools/vidsim.py timing --card v4 checks the table.
 1395 f8a9: 31          vcrtab: DB 49             ; R0  counts a line - 1
 1396 f8aa: 28                  DB 40             ; R1  counts shown: 80 characters
 1397 f8ab: 2a                  DB 42             ; R2  the horizontal sync from count 42
 1398 f8ac: 26                  DB 026h           ; R3  the horizontal sync 6 counts (96 dots); the vertical 2 lines on Hitachi's S type
 1399 f8ad: 1f                  DB 31             ; R4  vertical total - 1 (rows)
 1400 f8ae: 0d                  DB 13             ; R5  vertical total adjust (scan lines)
 1401 f8af: 19                  DB VROWS          ; R6  rows displayed
 1402 f8b0: 1c                  DB 28             ; R7  vertical sync position (row): line 448
 1403 f8b1: 00                  DB 0              ; R8  interlace mode: off
 1404 f8b2: 0f                  DB 15             ; R9  scan lines per row - 1
 1405 f8b3: 6e                  DB 06eh           ; R10 cursor start line 14, blinking (1/32 field rate)
 1406 f8b4: 0f                  DB 15             ; R11 cursor end line 15
 1407 f8b5: 00                  DB 0              ; R12 start address high (in counts)
 1408 f8b6: 00                  DB 0              ; R13 start address low
 1409 f8b7: 00                  DB 0              ; R14 cursor address high
 1410 f8b8: 00                  DB 0              ; R15 cursor address low
